    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-17" id="fn-17" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Southern Company Services receives up-front payments for studies and operating companies do not record any charges to these accounts. Costs are bore at system level. The only time an operating company would have anything to report on page 231 is when the charges exceed the amount collected and the customer does not reimburse Southern Company. Any study completed by an operating company and is under the OATT should be reported by that operating company on page 231.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-18" id="fn-18" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Southern Company Services receives up-front payments for studies and operating companies do not record any charges to these accounts. Costs are bore at system level. The only time an operating company would have anything to report on page 231 is when the charges exceed the amount collected and the customer does not reimburse Southern Company. Any study completed by an operating company and is under the OATT should be reported by that operating company on page 231.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-19" id="fn-19" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">In 1993 the Company adopted FASB Statement No. 109 Accounting for Income Taxes. The</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">changes to this account are not treated as amortization and are charged to FERC accounts 282 and 283.</span>
